    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/sourcing-and-contracts-specialist-crawley-wa-australia-5d79d81c-1b16-4de9-8b15-932a85069880": {
      "title": "Sourcing and Contracts Specialist",
      "description": "Sourcing and Contracts Specialist - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Sourcing and Contracts Specialist 524919 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 25 Nov 2026 Play a key role in delivering strategic procurement and sourcing initiatives across one of Australia's leading universities. Contribute to process improvement, contract management and tendering activities that drive value and compliance across the University. Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $108,413 – $120,287 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area Finance supports the University through the delivery of strategic financial advice, financial stewardship, procurement services, compliance oversight, and operational support. Working across the University's Financial Compliance, Financial Performance and Procurement pillars, the team partners with stakeholders at all levels to deliver efficient, compliant and value-driven outcomes. The Procurement team provides expert guidance on sourcing, tendering, supplier management and contract administration, supporting the University to achieve its strategic objectives while ensuring strong governance and procurement best practice. About the opportunity Coordinate end-to-end procurement and tender processes, including market engagement, documentation preparation, tender administration and stakeholder support. Support contract administration activities, including contract documentation, amendments, variations and maintenance of the University's central contracts register. Drive continuous improvement by analysing procurement processes, monitoring compliance, supporting e-Procurement initiatives, and contributing to procurement strategy and reporting. About you Relevant tertiary qualification or equivalent experience in procurement, purchasing, supply chain, commerce, business or a related discipline. Demonstrated experience in procurement operations, tendering, sourcing, contract administration and procurement systems. Strong stakeholder engagement, communication and relationship management skills, with the ability to work effectively across diverse groups. Well-developed analytical, problem-solving and organisational skills, with experience identifying and implementing process improvements. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and business systems, with the ability to work independently while contributing positively to a collaborative team environment. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Sourcing and Contracts Specialist - 524919.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Emma Gillespie at emma.gillespie@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday, 25 November 2025. The University reserves the right to interview and appoint a suitably qualified candidate prior to the closing date. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Senior Manager, Program Delivery Crawley, WA Business Development Lead a portfolio of programs and projects, delivering outcomes within scope, budget, timelines and governance requirements. Project Officer, Sustaining Capital Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Contribute to projects that sustain and enhance UWA's physical infrastructure and facilities environment through the delivery of asset replacement and renewal. Technical Assistant Crawley, WA Technical/Laboratory support Provides high-quality teaching and research support for the Biomedical Sciences platform based at the QEII Medical Centre, Nedlands. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/project-officer-sustaining-capital-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Project Officer, Sustaining Capital",
      "description": "Project Officer, Sustaining Capital - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Project Officer, Sustaining Capital 524819 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 18 Nov 2026 Contribute to projects that sustain and enhance UWA's physical infrastructure and facilities environment through the delivery of asset replacement and renewal. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $99,040 – $104,669 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Campus Management is responsible for the planning, development, management and operation of the University of Western Australia's physical estate and infrastructure. Through integrated property, facilities, asset management, capital works and operational services, the team delivers safe, sustainable and efficient environments that support teaching, research and campus life. Within Campus Management, the Capital Works and Delivery team leads the planning and delivery of infrastructure, asset renewal and capital investment programs that ensure UWA's campuses remain world-class environments for learning, discovery and community engagement. About the opportunity Support the delivery of sustaining capital projects, including physical asset lifecycle replacement and renewal programs and minor works projects across UWA's diverse property portfolio. Coordinate project planning, procurement, documentation, stakeholder engagement, contractor access and project administration throughout project lifecycle from initiation through to completion. Monitor project progress, budgets, schedules, risks and compliance requirements while working collaboratively with project managers, consultants, contractors and University stakeholders. About you Relevant tertiary qualification in project management, construction management, engineering, architecture, property, facilities management, finance or a related discipline, or demonstrated equivalent competency. Demonstrated experience supporting the delivery of construction, infrastructure, facilities, maintenance or capital works projects. Sound understanding of project management principles and practices. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple tasks and priorities while meeting deadlines. Experience assisting with procurement, contract administration and project financial management processes. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Project Officer, Sustaining Capital (524819).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Melita O'Donnell at melita.odonnell@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume (max. 4 pages) and Cover Letter (max. 2 pages) should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday, 25 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Senior Manager, Program Delivery Crawley, WA Business Development Lead a portfolio of programs and projects, delivering outcomes within scope, budget, timelines and governance requirements. Sourcing and Contracts Specialist Crawley, WA Finance Drive strategic sourcing, tendering and contract management at UWA, delivering value, compliance and continuous improvement. Technical Assistant Crawley, WA Technical/Laboratory support Provides high-quality teaching and research support for the Biomedical Sciences platform based at the QEII Medical Centre, Nedlands. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
