    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/associate-professor-pharmacy-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Associate Professor (Pharmacy)",
      "description": "Associate Professor (Pharmacy) - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Associate Professor (Pharmacy) 524933 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 19 Nov 2026 Provide academic leadership in a growing pharmacy discipline that is shaping the future of pharmacist education, research and practice. Join a collaborative, research-intensive environment with opportunities to build national and international partnerships and deliver real-world health impact. Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a tenurable basis. Base salary range: Level D, $179,945.00 – $197,969.00 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Department of Pharmacy within the School of Health and Clinical Sciences at The University of Western Australia delivers innovative postgraduate pharmacy education and research focused on medicines optimisation and improving health outcomes. Working closely with patients, healthcare professionals, researchers and health systems, the Department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, student supervision and community engagement within a culturally safe and inclusive environment. About the opportunity Provide academic leadership across teaching, curriculum development, assessment and research supervision within the Doctor of Pharmacy and related programs. Lead impactful pharmacy research, secure competitive funding, build collaborative research partnerships and contribute to the University's national and international research reputation. Drive strategic initiatives across research education, student research projects, curriculum innovation, professional engagement and academic governance. About you PhD in a discipline relevant to pharmacy, with a strong record of academic leadership in teaching, learning and curriculum innovation. Demonstrated success in supervising substantial student research projects and higher degree research candidates, with evidence of quality completions and research outputs. An established research profile evidenced by high-quality publications, competitive research funding success and the ability to lead collaborative research programs. Proven ability to build and maintain partnerships with universities, industry, government and professional stakeholders that enhance research impact and educational outcomes. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive teaching practices, mentoring academic colleagues, and contributing positively to team, School and University initiatives. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD Associate Professor Pharmacy (524933).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Liza Seubert at liza.seubert@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at Pratik.Sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday, November 19 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Postdoctoral Research Associate Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, Science Investigate black hole origins and galaxy evolution using cutting-edge models, simulations and supercomputing resources. Postdoctoral Research Associate (Jim Buckee Fellowship) Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, Science Lead independent SKA-focused astrophysics research within a world-class astronomy centre with access to leading supercomputing resources. Associate Lecturer (Pharmacy) Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Help shape the next generation of pharmacists through teaching, assessment and placement learning in a supportive academic team at UWA. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/project-analyst-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Project Analyst",
      "description": "Project Analyst - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Project Analyst 524911 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 26 Nov 2026 Contribute to the successful delivery of enterprise-wide strategic initiatives that shape the future direction of UWA. Join a high-performing team supporting strategy execution, governance, planning and institutional transformation across the University. Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $99,040 – $104,669 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor, Planning and Strategic Initiatives supports the University’s strategic direction and institutional performance through enterprise-wide strategy, planning, governance and oversight of major strategic programs. Within this portfolio, the University Program Office (UPO) plays a critical role in enabling the successful delivery of strategic initiatives across the University. The team provides project governance, portfolio oversight, reporting, assurance, planning frameworks and delivery support that help turn strategic priorities into measurable outcomes. About the opportunity Provide project analysis, governance coordination, reporting and delivery support across a portfolio of high-impact strategic programs and initiatives. Develop and maintain project plans, dashboards, governance documentation, reporting packs and portfolio insights that support informed decision-making and program performance. Partner with Program Directors, Project Managers, Change Managers and stakeholders across the University to identify risks, dependencies and opportunities while contributing to continuous improvement of project management and governance practices. About you Relevant tertiary qualification, or equivalent experience, in project management, business, commerce, strategy, information management or a related discipline. Demonstrated experience supporting projects, programs, portfolio management activities or organisational improvement initiatives within a complex environment. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to interpret data, synthesise information from multiple sources and identify emerging risks, issues and dependencies. Excellent written, verbal and stakeholder engagement skills, with experience preparing reports, dashboards, briefing papers, presentations and governance documentation. Strong organisational skills, digital capability and attention to detail, with the ability to manage competing priorities and work collaboratively across diverse stakeholder groups. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: Project Analyst - 524911.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Chris Wever at chris.wever@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday, 26 November 2026. The University reserves the right to interview and appoint a suitably qualified candidate prior to the closing date. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Postdoctoral Research Associate Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, Science Investigate black hole origins and galaxy evolution using cutting-edge models, simulations and supercomputing resources. Postdoctoral Research Associate (Jim Buckee Fellowship) Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, Science Lead independent SKA-focused astrophysics research within a world-class astronomy centre with access to leading supercomputing resources. Associate Lecturer (Pharmacy) Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Help shape the next generation of pharmacists through teaching, assessment and placement learning in a supportive academic team at UWA. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/associate-lecturer-pharmacy-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer (Pharmacy)",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer (Pharmacy) - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Associate Lecturer (Pharmacy) 524928 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 19 Nov 2026 Help shape the next generation of pharmacists through high-quality teaching, assessment and Work Integrated Learning (WIL) experiences. Join a collaborative and supportive academic team within a leading Group of Eight university. Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a tenurable basis. Base salary range: Level A, $86,839.00 – $116,866.00 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The University of Western Australia's School of Health and Clinical Sciences delivers innovative, high-quality education and research across a broad range of health disciplines and is committed to improving health outcomes through culturally safe, inclusive teaching, learning and community engagement. Within the School, the Department of Pharmacy delivers postgraduate pharmacy education, including the Doctor of Pharmacy and advanced pharmacy practice programs. The Department works closely with patients, healthcare professionals and healthcare systems to advance medicines optimisation through education, collaboration and professional practice. About the opportunity Support the delivery of high-quality pharmacy education through tutorials, practical classes, simulation-based learning and online teaching activities across postgraduate pharmacy programs. Contribute to student assessment, Work Integrated Learning (WIL) activities and placement support, including preparation of learning materials, marking, feedback and engagement with placement supervisors. Develop your academic career within a supportive environment, working closely with experienced pharmacy educators while contributing to continuous improvement, student success and culturally safe learning practices. About you A pharmacy qualification together with experience practising as a pharmacist and current registration, or eligibility for registration, with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) in Western Australia. Demonstrated ability to contribute to innovative, student-centred teaching and learning, including the development of teaching resources and assessment activities. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build effective relationships with students, academic colleagues and healthcare professionals. An understanding of student assessment and pharmacy placements, with a commitment to developing expertise in Work Integrated Learning, assessment and curriculum delivery. Commitment to inclusion, equity, diversity and culturally safe educational practices, with the ability to contribute positively to a collaborative academic environment. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Occasional travel within Western Australia and interstate may be required. Position description: PD Associate Lecturer Pharmacy (524928).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Liza Seubert at liza.seubert@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at Pratik.Sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday 19 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Postdoctoral Research Associate Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, Science Investigate black hole origins and galaxy evolution using cutting-edge models, simulations and supercomputing resources. Postdoctoral Research Associate (Jim Buckee Fellowship) Crawley, WA Engineering and Mathematical Sciences, Science Lead independent SKA-focused astrophysics research within a world-class astronomy centre with access to leading supercomputing resources. Associate Professor (Pharmacy) Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Drive strategic initiatives across research education, student research projects, curriculum innovation, professional engagement and academic governance. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
