    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-medical-school-year-1-clinical-skills-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Medical School – Year 1 Clinical Skills",
      "description": "Lecturer - Medical School – Year 1 Clinical Skills - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Lecturer - Medical School – Year 1 Clinical Skills 524869 Crawley, WA Part Time Closing on: 30 Nov 2026 Part-time (0.1 FTE) appointment on a tenurable basis. Clinical loading is applicable. Base salary range: Level B, $122,876 – $145,404 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The UWA Medical School is the largest and longest-established medical school in Western Australia, delivering a world-class four-year postgraduate Doctor of Medicine (MD) program to local, national and international students. The School is recognised for its strong teaching and research programs across a broad range of medical disciplines. Within the School, the Discipline of General Practice delivers innovative, high-quality education in partnership with the wider medical profession and general practice community, preparing students for contemporary clinical practice About the opportunity Deliver and lead small-group teaching, supervision and assessment within the Year 1 Clinical Skills curriculum, helping students develop core capabilities in clinical communication, history taking, physical examination and clinical reasoning. Facilitate engaging learning experiences using tutorials, simulated patients, peer learning activities and seminars across areas including cardiovascular, respiratory, gastrointestinal, renal and sexual health assessment. Contribute to Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs) and broader Medical School teaching and assessment activities, supporting excellence in medical education across the MD program. About you Unconditional registration with AHPRA as a Medical Practitioner in Western Australia. Extensive clinical practice experience, with broad expertise in patient assessment, history taking and physical examination across body systems. Experience teaching, supervising or mentoring medical students, junior doctors and/or other healthcare learners in a clinical or educational setting. Strong communication, interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage and support diverse learners. Well-developed organisational and collaboration skills, with a commitment to high-quality, student-centred medical education. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD [Lecturer] [524869].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Nahal Mavaddat at nahal.mavaddat@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Petrina Gomez at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday, 30 November 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working 