    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-medical-school-year-2-clinical-skills-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Medical School – Year 2 Clinical Skills",
      "description": "Lecturer - Medical School – Year 2 Clinical Skills - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Lecturer - Medical School – Year 2 Clinical Skills 524867 Crawley, WA Part Time Closing on: 30 Nov 2026 Clinical loading is applicable. Part-time (0.1 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis.. Base salary range: Level B, $122,876 – $145,404 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. Appointment commencing in late-January 2027 and concluding at the end of May 2027. About the area The UWA Medical School is the largest and longest-established medical school in Western Australia, delivering a world-class four-year postgraduate Doctor of Medicine (MD) program to local, national and international students. The School is recognised for its strong teaching and research programs across a broad range of medical disciplines. Within the School, the Discipline of General Practice delivers innovative, high-quality education in partnership with the wider medical profession and general practice community, preparing students for contemporary clinical practice. About the opportunity Deliver engaging small-group teaching and assessment activities within the MD Year 2 Clinical Preparation program, supporting students to develop core clinical examination, history-taking and clinical reasoning skills. Facilitate learning through tutorials, simulated patient encounters and practical clinical skills sessions with a focus on musculoskeletal and neurological examination. Contribute to Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs), broader teaching activities and School initiatives that support excellence in medical education. About you Unconditional registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA) as a Medical Practitioner in Western Australia. Extensive clinical practice experience, with broad expertise in patient assessment, history taking and examination across body systems. Demonstrated experience teaching, supervising or mentoring medical students and/or junior doctors in clinical environments. Strong communication, interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to engage and support diverse learners. Highly developed organisational skills and a commitment to delivering high-quality, student-centred medical education. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD [Lecturer] [524867].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Nahal Mavaddat at nahal.mavaddat@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Petrina Gomez at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Monday, 30 November 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs School Operations Officer Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services Join a collaborative team delivering high-quality operational and administrative support to academics, researchers and students. Senior Lecturer - Medical School – Year 2 Students Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Deliver high-impact clinical skills education within UWA's Doctor of Medicine (MD) program, focusing on patient assessment, clinical reasoning, and examination skills. Senior Lecturer - Medical School – Year 1 Clinical Skills Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Play a key role in shaping the next generation of medical practitioners through high-quality clinical skills education. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/program-director-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Program Director",
      "description": "Program Director - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Program Director 525043 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 3 Dec 2026 Focus on strategic enterprise-wide programs at UWA. Influence executive decision-making and shape long-term institutional outcomes. Full-time appointment on an ongoing basis. Competitive salary package including 17% superannuation. About the area The University Program Office sits within the Office of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Planning and Strategic Initiatives) and plays a critical role in driving the University’s strategic priorities. The portfolio provides leadership in strategy execution, planning, governance, and performance oversight to ensure major institutional initiatives deliver meaningful outcomes for the University community. This is a unique opportunity to impact strategic programs that will help shape the future direction, capability, and performance of one of Australia's leading universities. About the opportunity Provide end-to-end leadership and accountability for a major strategic program, translating institutional priorities into a coordinated and deliverable program of work. Lead multiple interconnected projects and multidisciplinary teams, ensuring successful delivery of program outcomes, benefits realisation, governance, risk management, financial performance, and organisational change. Partner with Executive Sponsors, senior leaders, governance committees, and external stakeholders to drive strategic alignment, influence decision-making, and deliver enterprise-wide transformation outcomes. About you Relevant postgraduate qualifications or equivalent senior leadership experience in program management, transformation, strategy, business management, or a related discipline. Extensive experience leading large-scale, complex transformation programs or strategic initiatives within a sizeable and multifaceted organisation. Demonstrated expertise in program governance, assurance, risk management, stakeholder engagement, and benefits realisation. Strong commercial and financial acumen, with experience overseeing substantial budgets, resource planning, and external service providers. Exceptional communication, influencing, and executive stakeholder management skills, with a proven ability to navigate complexity, drive outcomes, and lead across organisational boundaries. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance and Finance Check will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Program Director 525043.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Chris Wever at chris.wever@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Wendy Young at wendy.young@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday, 3 December 2026 Please note that UWA may begin the recruitment process and conduct interviews prior to the advertised closing date. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs School Operations Officer Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services Join a collaborative team delivering high-quality operational and administrative support to academics, researchers and students. Senior Lecturer - Medical School – Year 2 Students Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Deliver high-impact clinical skills education within UWA's Doctor of Medicine (MD) program, focusing on patient assessment, clinical reasoning, and examination skills. Senior Lecturer - Medical School – Year 1 Clinical Skills Crawley, WA Health and Medical Sciences Play a key role in shaping the next generation of medical practitioners through high-quality clinical skills education. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
